For hidden food probability p, P(positive worth)=e+(1-2e)*p.
If forced to choose one of two equally costly colours, choose p>1/2.
If abstention is available, positive expected meal gain requires e+(1-2e)*p>2/3.
At e>=1/3 no p<=1 yields strictly positive expected scored meal gain.
This concerns the existing food-minus-two-poison numerator, not a new survival objective.
